\section{Build and render}{

In a terminal, in the site folder, build the image and give it a name:

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode">}}\preformatted{docker build -t my-supplement .
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

Then render one report in it with the site folder mounted at \verb{/site}.
On macOS and Linux:

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode">}}\preformatted{docker run --rm --network none --user "$(id -u):$(id -g)" -e HOME=/tmp \\
